title ALES145 — Lotus's stereo_zero_cross: the zero-crossing counter carried into stereo, the suite's first STEREO ANALYSIS rung, one shared band and two independent counters
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Second lap of this recur turn (after ALES144 stereo_schmitt). Crux-first, the natural next member is ALES93's zero_cross — the analysis SIBLING that reads schmitt's rail flips as a count. Where ALES144 carried the trigger's WRITE into stereo, this carries its READ: the suite's first STEREO ANALYSIS rung. It pairs with the stereo meter (ALES17), the only other stereo reader, so the analysis corner now holds two members (level and activity).
think ALES93 counts rail flips (a zero crossing in the hysteresis sense) without writing a sample, carrying both the trigger rail AND the previous output rail so a flip at a seam is counted exactly once. Carried into stereo, each channel carries its own counter, so the two counts are INDEPENDENT — an identical-channel master reads equal counts, a busy channel over a calm one counts more. The crux (split-equals-whole) carries up one level, in stereo: a two-piece StereoZeroCounter count equals the whole counted once on BOTH channels, each seam flip counted once per channel.
think Mirrored ALES93's two forms: count_crossings_stereo (from silence, returns StereoCrossings{left,right}) and StereoZeroCounter (two ZeroCounters on one shared band via a single init so left/right can't drift). Reused ALES93's ZeroCrossError whole (BadThreshold/BadRange/CountFull) and ALES92's precheck for the one-up-front validation, so a refusal never counts one channel and moves the other's state.
think Proved all four laws: the stereo zero-cross law against ALES93's own count_crossings per channel; the read-only/balance law (source byte-for-byte unchanged on both, pair balanced); the independent-counter law (identical reads equal, busy-vs-calm 5 vs 0, chatter suppressed on each, in-band-only zero on both); and the carried-state/atomicity/degenerate law (two-piece = whole on both with a flip at the seam on each channel counted once, inverted band / bad range atomic with both counters untouched, count 0 the identity). The seam-flip case used opposite-phase alternating channels so both count 7 with a flip landing exactly at split index 4.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, read-only software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. The stereo ANALYSIS corner now holds level (ALES17 meter) and activity (ALES145 zero-cross) — a keeper reads two per-channel numbers apart. The honest lesson: an analysis rung's stereo lift is the same shape as an edit's (run the mono per channel, one shared parameter, validate once) yet the invariant flips from balance-of-writes to read-only-of-source. Witness GREEN (four laws), tame_style_check bans clean. Two rounds landed and sent this turn (ALES144-145), both crux-first continuations of the comparator class into stereo. The next Lotus lap opens a fresh heading — another mono primitive into stereo, or a new corner.
